course: dictionary
lesson: 12987
title: Money words: expense
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An expense is money that you spend, or have to pay, on something. «The new bike was a big expense for our family.» The bike cost a lot of money, so it was a big expense.
explain: Expense is a noun. You can have one expense, or several expenses. «Our biggest expense each month is the rent.» Each expense is money the family must pay out.
explain: Watch for the phrase «at someone's expense». It can mean they paid for something, or that a joke made them look silly. «The clown fell into the pond, and everyone laughed at his expense.» Nobody paid for anything here: the clown was made to look silly.
fact: An expense is something you have to pay for.
fact: Expense means the amount of money something costs.
fact: Expenses are money a worker spends for the job and is paid back for, such as travel expenses.
fact: «At someone's expense» can mean they paid for it, or that a joke made them look silly.
fact: In maths, income minus expenses shows how much money is left over.
exercise: «Our biggest expense each month is the rent.» What is an expense? | Money someone gives you as a present | *Money you spend or have to pay for | A happy feeling | A kind of bird
exercise: A worker spends money on a train trip for the job, and the company pays them back. What are these costs called? | Presents | *Expenses that are paid back | Holidays | Expenses
exercise: «The clown fell into the pond, and everyone laughed at his expense.» What does «at his expense» show? | He won a prize | He was given a bath | *He was made to look silly | He paid for a new hat
test: «The new roof was a huge expense, but we had saved for it.» What does expense mean here? | A holiday | *The cost of something | Happy news | A type of tree
test: «Everyone laughed at the mayor's expense when his umbrella blew inside out.» What does this mean? | *He was made to look silly | He paid for the umbrella | He sent everyone a letter | He was given a prize
exam: Maya's shop has income of 500 pounds and expenses of 320 pounds. How much is left over? | 820 pounds | 500 pounds | 320 pounds | *180 pounds
